One acceptable fix was to have the reduction produce its (64‐bit) result in an X register rather than a W register. In SVE the reduction (ADDV) “sums‐across” the lanes using the vector’s “active element size” (which is determined by the predicate) but the result is always written in a full 64‐bit register. (In many examples you’ll see “addv x0, p0, z0” even when you loaded 32‐bit values.) In our original code the instruction

