    //   cntw  – to count active lanes in a predicate
    //   dup   – to replicate a scalar constant into a vector register
    //   ld1d/st1d – to load/store 64-bit elements from/to memory
    //   neg   – to negate vector elements (used here twice as a no‐op)
    //   and   – to “mask” the result with an all–ones immediate.
    // Finally it calls printf to show a confirmation string.
