Below is one acceptable corrected version. In our solution we make the following changes:

1. The SVE “cntw” and “cnth” instructions do not accept the token “ALL” but do accept the lowercase “all” as the predicate‐constraint.
2. Both the “and (immediate)” and “lsr (immediate)” instructions are “destructive” – that is, the destination must be the same as the source. Therefore we first copy z0 into another register (z1 for the bitwise AND and z2 for lsr) and then apply the instruction “in‐place”. (For example, one cannot write “and z1.d, z0.d, #…” but must instead do “mov z1.d, z0.d” then “and z1.d, z1.d, #…”.)
